;; zde - the input layer.
;;
;; niri binds one modifier set plus one key. Everything the keymap wants that
;; is not that shape lives here: a key held as a layer, and later the leader
;; sequences and the modes (docs/roadmap.md, 0.2).
;;
;; It does not know about zde. It rewrites physical keys into keys no keyboard
;; has - F13 upwards - and niri binds those like any other. The chord a person
;; presses is written next to the bind in common/keymap/keymap.yaml as its
;; `via`, and that is what the cheatsheet shows.
;;
;; This file is checked at build time: the NixOS module runs kanata --check
;; over it, so a config that does not parse fails the build rather than the
;; session. What it cannot check is whether the keys do the right thing, which
;; wants a keyboard (docs/roadmap.md, verify list).

(defsrc
  tab j k up down)

(deflayer base
  @tab j k up down)

;; Held Tab walks this desk's band. j and k are the vim axis, the arrows are
;; the same thing for a hand that is not on home row. Tapped, Tab is Tab: the
;; switcher is Mod+Tab and stays that way.
(deflayer band
  _ f13 f14 f14 f13)

(defalias
  ;; 200ms to decide. Below that a fast typist's Tab starts a layer; well above
  ;; it, Tab feels sticky. It is the number to change first if either happens.
  tab (tap-hold 200 200 tab (layer-while-held band)))
